Title: F2-M03 — The Last Ferry (briefing)
Credit: Staalfront
Author: Staalfront narrative team
Draft date: 2026-10-17

> FADE IN:

INT. FERRY HOUSE, SOUTH SHORE - OVERCAST MORNING

[[AMBIENCE: water slapping against pilings, gulls, a truck idling outside]]
[[MUSIC: sparse, cold piano under tension]]

A lake chart is spread across the ferry master's desk. COMMANDER SAVA and DRAVEC stand over it. Through the window, the far shore is a grey line.

DRAVEC
(alert)
The ferry has families aboard and a crew that refused to abandon them. Enemy scouts are closing on the shore.

[[SHOT: map]]
[[MAP: lake with north pier and ferry marked; south landing in marsh; east road and headland shore track as enemy approaches; marsh road to evacuation camp]]

DRAVEC
North pier to our landing is four minutes across open water. The landing is marsh: a picket in it, five rifles, a scout, one light tank. Then the east road behind that.

COMMANDER SAVA
(measured)
We have one transport and a small escort. There is no time to bring the full column around the lake.

COMMANDER SAVA
(clipped)
The risk is the water. If a tank reaches the bank while she is still out there, the families die in the lake and we watch it. Rockets on the armour first.

DRAVEC
Eight people. Five to a truck. That is two runs or two trucks, and the marsh road is slow either way.

COMMANDER SAVA
(firm)
Open the shoreline route, repair the ferry engine, and escort everyone to the evacuation point.

DRAVEC
(worried)
The crew say she has not run that engine in a week, Commander. Keep the engineer close to the bank. Just in case.

[[SFX: radio click]]
[[MUSIC: stop]]

> FADE OUT.
